A||N||4||trigger||where to find an engine management system that works with the Fiero||||5||
Z||000000||trigger||06-12-2001||07:54 PM||||I am seriously considering building a twin turbo 2.5, 5 speed this summer.  The car is a 1987 pontiac fiero coupe.  It has the 5 speed and no options.  I believe it has a/c and that's it.  I want to find an engine management system that will make the car run.  I know that somebody asked if 350 pistons fit in a 2.5, and I would like to know it this actually works, or if somebody knows where I can find forged pistons for the 2.5?  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Steve Normington||06-12-2001||08:27 PM||||I was looking at HalTech's <A HREF="http://www.haltech.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.haltech.com</A>  E6K engine management system ($1.5 - 2.0K). As long as you keep the Fiero trigger and ignition module, it should work. The E6K is spark and fuel controller, it will hook up to the GM TPS, IAC, injectors, and can batch fire 6 injectors and run a waste spark DIS system.<P>------------------<BR>I don't car if my next Fiero is a 2M Hamster, I'm not swapping the engine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MoneypitGT||06-12-2001||08:42 PM||||If you are looking for something non-stand alone try the Apex stuff. That is what I am going to try when ever I get the turbo QUAD done (hopefully by fall). Their AVCR and the boost controller. <A HREF="http://www.apexi.com" TARGET=_blank>www.apexi.com</A> <BR>  Chris<P>------------------<BR><B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>2 '87 GT Projects||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||06-12-2001||09:27 PM||||The Holley Commander 950 gets my vote, and it's a lot cheaper than a Haltech.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Terrybogin||06-12-2001||09:52 PM||||A '749 ecm from a turbo sunbird/quad-4/GMC Syclone will work fine. Get the schematic for the Fiero and GMC ecm's pinouts and swap the wires to the correct place for the new ECM (they are even the correct color!) Get the cheap pocket programmer and prom eraser from xtronics and download Programmer98 from the SY/TY website. You will only have to add a knock sensor and wire for it and a 2 bar MAP. If you want to go DIS, get the ecm and prom for a 91 turbo Grand Prix, it is in a "weather proof case" (p/n '727). You can buy GMEPro, winbin or TunerCat to edit the 727 code. The biggie with a GM ecm is it will retain "limp home mode", something I know first hand that Holley does not have- a defective o2 sensor left me sitting on the side of the road!||||reg||1
